;B[pd];W[cq];B[qo];W[cc];B[dp];W[cp];B[do];W[er];B[dd];W[dc]LB[cd:A]C[To play at 'A' would be unthinkable, leaving white very one-sided.]
;B[ed];W[be];B[gp]C[It is clear in which direction the game is going - black plays for influence and white goes for territory. Black goes straight for his objective but maybe ties himslef down too quickly.]
;W[df]LB[id:B]C[A play at 'B' is another possibility.];B[jd];W[qj];B[qh]C[Black can also make a shimari at 20.]
;W[pq];B[op];W[oq];B[np];W[mq];B[mp];W[lq];B[lp];W[nq]C[Very bad. This has no effect on black at all. It should be replaced by 38.]
;B[pj];W[pk];B[oj];W[qi];B[ph];W[ql];B[ol];W[on]C[Incomprehensible. White should by all means live with a move such as 39.]
;B[pm];W[ro];B[qm];W[qp]C[Should be replaced with by a move one point to the right of 37 to live.]
;B[qn]C[White still has aji to live with the sagari to the right of 32 after this move. Black should play sagari to the right of 37 instead.]
;W[lc];B[le];W[pc];B[oc];W[qc];B[nd]C[The solid connection is better.];W[qd];B[qe]
;W[qf];B[pe];W[re];B[pf];W[rg];B[rh];W[hd];B[if]LB[he:C]C[The tsuke at 'C' is a more severe way of playing. It is a good idea for black to give up the two stones, but black must make good use of them, else the white corner will become too big.]
;W[hf];B[hg];W[gf];B[jp]C[This is a very poor move - completely unnecessary. Black must complete his formation with 80 or 64.]
;W[hi];B[ji];W[ie]C[Bad shape and aji-keshi. White loses the possibility of a connection at 95.]
;B[je];W[ig];B[jf];W[dl];B[dq];W[dr];B[co];W[hk];B[cr];W[br];B[bq]C[This exchange is not too proffitable for black.]
;W[bp];B[bo];W[aq];B[fl];W[jj];B[ih];W[gg];B[kj];W[jk];B[hh];W[gh];B[fj];W[ki];B[kh]
;W[li];B[mj];W[in]C[This move us too small, and should be replaced by 91. 91 would preserve the territory on the left and also prevent the cut below 84.]
;B[dj];W[ll];B[lj];W[ic];B[jc];W[jb];B[jm];W[gn];B[fm];W[jn];B[hm];W[im];B[hl];W[ko]
;B[kp];W[ii];B[jh];W[gi];B[kb];W[hb]C[There is no reason why the solid connection at 114 should not be played.]
;B[rn]LB[ri:B][rk:C][rm:A]C[This move is extremely large. Without it, white still has aji to live by playing 'A' and 'B' in sente, and then at 'C' to start a ko. One gets the impression that white should have made more of these stones than he did in the actual game.]
;W[dh]C[Far too slow. The correct way is to play tsuke at 189. White would find it hard to deal with such a move.]
;B[ja];W[ib]C[17-18\: Neither of these moves is correct. the biggest area from the point of view of yose is concerned with the tsuke at 189.]
;B[pb];W[qb];B[nb];W[rp];B[qa];W[ra];B[pa];W[sb]LB[rc:D]C[It is far better to connect at 'D'. This would also defend the weak point at 96.]
;B[ci]C[As emphacised above, this is a very large point.];W[bh];B[ch];W[bg];B[cg]
;W[cf];B[dg]C[Not so big. Better to play at 214.];W[na];B[ob];W[kc];B[lb];W[mb]
