;B[ma];W[ao];B[an];W[ap];B[bm];W[mb];B[ar];W[as];B[ma];W[jr]C[This move is not big enough. A white play at 104 would be much better. Note also that 171 is a ko threat for both players, and should certainly have been played by this stage. 
(White would threaten to break into black's territory by playing ate at 189.) Had white played 171 or 204 here, he would still have a chance to win. ]
;B[ka];W[iq];B[ln];W[ip]C[A wasted move for white. He should connect at 163, for even if black pulls out at 166, white can still connect at 162, As compared with the game, his gain on the left is seen to outweigh his loss on the right.]
